From: OP15 infiniti camera port
Subject: [PATCH] TypeFaceUtil: catch NPE from absent OplusBaseConfiguration.mOplusExtraConfiguration

OOS-restore (facilitation, contract-gap closer). On a OnePlus device the
custom font path resolves Configuration -> OplusBaseConfiguration ->
mOplusExtraConfiguration -> mFontVariationSettings. On LineageOS the OnePlus
framework does not populate mOplusExtraConfiguration, so the iget at the
"->mFontVariationSettings:I" read NPEs. The existing try only catches
NoSuchFieldError / NoSuchMethodError, so the NullPointerException escapes and
crashes the camera on open (US-001), and -- because OplusTextView.<init> calls
this same TypeFaceUtil method -- it also surfaces as the ai_hint_layout
InflateException when the AI-scene hint UI inflates OplusTextView.

The :catch_0 handler already falls back to Typeface.DEFAULT (the same graceful
result OnePlus yields when the extra-config is absent), so routing
NullPointerException to it restores OOS behaviour without forcing or disabling
the custom-font path.

Anchor: fingerprint on the field ref
"Loplus/content/res/OplusFontUtils;->isFlipFontUsed:Z" followed by the existing
NoSuchFieldError/NoSuchMethodError catches to :catch_0 (structural, not line
numbers). Class s7/m3 is apktool's deterministic obfuscation of TypeFaceUtil
for the committed OplusCamera.apk; regenerate if the APK is updated.
--- a/smali/s7/m3.smali
+++ b/smali/s7/m3.smali
@@ -347,6 +347,7 @@
     :try_end_0
     .catch Ljava/lang/NoSuchFieldError; {:try_start_0 .. :try_end_0} :catch_0
     .catch Ljava/lang/NoSuchMethodError; {:try_start_0 .. :try_end_0} :catch_0
+    .catch Ljava/lang/NullPointerException; {:try_start_0 .. :try_end_0} :catch_0
 
     .line 40
     .line 41
